WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.371 --> 00:00:01.572
- Question.

00:00:01.572 --> 00:00:03.812
How much of this is all gonna be public?

00:00:03.812 --> 00:00:05.125
Like if I write in there about

00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:07.235
my deepest, darkest fantasies,

00:00:07.235 --> 00:00:09.048
will this be displayed
to the people of YouTube?

00:00:09.048 --> 00:00:14.048
(upbeat piano music)

00:00:23.504 --> 00:00:25.824
- So I was thinking about
my first time journaling,

00:00:25.824 --> 00:00:27.704
and I was in sixth grade,

00:00:27.704 --> 00:00:28.704
and I'd written this journal,

00:00:28.704 --> 00:00:29.638
and my friends found the journal,

00:00:29.638 --> 00:00:31.291
and read it out loud,

00:00:31.291 --> 00:00:33.021
and laughed at me,

00:00:33.021 --> 00:00:34.409
so I through the journal in the trash.

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:36.841
- I kept several journals as a child.

00:00:36.841 --> 00:00:39.871
I would write who my crush was,

00:00:39.871 --> 00:00:42.106
and what I wanted to do to my enemy.

00:00:42.106 --> 00:00:43.971
- I'm coming in as a grown woman,

00:00:43.971 --> 00:00:46.254
with no journaling experience.

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:48.138
- I had this rad Farrari notebook,

00:00:48.138 --> 00:00:51.357
and like every other
journal I've ever had,

00:00:51.357 --> 00:00:53.698
I did about three entries,

00:00:53.698 --> 00:00:55.739
and then that was the last entry.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:57.138
- Kinda hoping that maybe I'll at least

00:00:57.138 --> 00:00:58.555
fill up half the book.

00:00:58.555 --> 00:00:59.984
- I'm excited to journal,

00:00:59.984 --> 00:01:02.374
because this is gonna be retribution

00:01:02.374 --> 00:01:03.948
for my stolen journal,

00:01:03.948 --> 00:01:05.955
when I was abroad, in college.

00:01:07.035 --> 00:01:09.142
- [Allison] Olay, it's journal time.

00:01:09.142 --> 00:01:10.822
I'm in my bedroom.

00:01:11.272 --> 00:01:13.002
There's my journal.

00:01:14.482 --> 00:01:16.228
It's happening!

00:01:16.368 --> 00:01:18.629
- I'm hanging out in
the back of my mini-van,

00:01:18.629 --> 00:01:20.288
and I'm about to do

00:01:20.288 --> 00:01:21.948
my first entry,

00:01:22.978 --> 00:01:25.688
in my journal.

00:01:25.688 --> 00:01:27.446
- So far, it's been kinda tough

00:01:27.446 --> 00:01:30.076
cuz I'm outta practice, my hand hurts,

00:01:30.076 --> 00:01:32.416
and I'm not exactly sure

00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:33.901
what I'm supposed to be writing about.

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:37.113
- I have usually been journaling so far,

00:01:37.113 --> 00:01:39.746
in the evenings, in my dining room,

00:01:39.746 --> 00:01:41.379
which is where I am now.

00:01:41.379 --> 00:01:43.501
- Hmm. I haven't been doing that well.

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:44.794
I'm gonna be honest.

00:01:44.794 --> 00:01:48.364
- (energizing music)

00:01:48.364 --> 00:01:49.869
- [Colin] I spend way too
much time sitting there going,

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:52.661
"I should be journaling!
I should be journaling!"

00:01:52.661 --> 00:01:54.128
Don't you guys do that?

00:01:54.128 --> 00:01:55.444
- Oh. It just comes out.

00:01:55.444 --> 00:01:57.631
It's like word vomit for me,

00:01:57.631 --> 00:01:58.561
and drawing vomit.

00:01:58.561 --> 00:02:00.069
I'm just like all over
the place in this thing.

00:02:00.069 --> 00:02:02.406
And then my cat plays with this string,

00:02:02.406 --> 00:02:03.761
and it's so cute and amazing.

00:02:03.761 --> 00:02:04.661
(laughter)

00:02:04.661 --> 00:02:06.673
- At first, it was like, what
do I want to write about?

00:02:06.673 --> 00:02:08.861
And then it's just kinda
like coming out of me.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:12.591
- I mean, it is interesting
to have a journal,

00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:17.061
which feels like the
offline, most inner thoughts,

00:02:17.061 --> 00:02:21.361
versus like all the social
media that I work in.

00:02:21.361 --> 00:02:23.311
- "To me it's seems like
Instagram and Twitter,

00:02:23.311 --> 00:02:25.361
"and all of those things
are such a carefully,

00:02:25.361 --> 00:02:26.878
"architectured version of how someone

00:02:26.878 --> 00:02:28.284
"wants to present their life.

00:02:28.284 --> 00:02:30.321
"And journaling,
essentially, at least for me,

00:02:30.321 --> 00:02:32.168
"about the messy, complicated,

00:02:32.168 --> 00:02:33.328
"not-so-sunny thoughts."

00:02:33.328 --> 00:02:36.831
- You know, Hillary got that journaling

00:02:36.831 --> 00:02:38.531
versus Instagram thing in my head,

00:02:38.531 --> 00:02:40.033
and I haven't stopped thinking about that.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:40.968
And she's totally right.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:44.114
It's very, very introspective.

00:02:44.114 --> 00:02:45.575
- Journaling is the opposite of Instagram.

00:02:45.575 --> 00:02:47.445
and I've never journaled before,

00:02:47.445 --> 00:02:49.310
and I've definitely Instagrammed before.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.702
And it's interesting to
do both, in the same day.

00:02:52.702 --> 00:02:54.195
- I'm a journaler at heart.

00:02:54.195 --> 00:02:56.823
It's just a way to create every day,

00:02:56.823 --> 00:02:58.587
in some type a way.

00:02:58.587 --> 00:03:00.429
"When did you stop dancing?"

00:03:00.429 --> 00:03:01.933
"When did you stop singing?"

00:03:01.933 --> 00:03:04.131
"When did you stop being
enchanted by stories?"

00:03:04.131 --> 00:03:06.000
"When did you stop finding comfort

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.131
in the sweet territory of silence?"

00:03:08.131 --> 00:03:09.967
I think the question
I would ask myself is,

00:03:09.967 --> 00:03:12.120
"When did you stop creating?"

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.463
I'm enjoying just kinda taking

00:03:15.463 --> 00:03:16.758
this time for myself every day.

00:03:16.758 --> 00:03:18.428
- So I've been journaling a lot

00:03:18.428 --> 00:03:21.228
in my van, parked places.

00:03:21.228 --> 00:03:22.261
I like to do it,

00:03:22.261 --> 00:03:25.761
cuz new environment is kinda inspiring.

00:03:25.761 --> 00:03:28.305
- My boyfriend is recording
with his band right now,

00:03:28.305 --> 00:03:31.341
and I'm doodling in my journal.

00:03:31.341 --> 00:03:33.861
It's really fun to draw
and write in my journal,

00:03:33.861 --> 00:03:37.550
while I'm around such
creative and inspiring people.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.060
- So I think I'm getting
a little bit better

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.401
at this journaling thing.

00:03:40.401 --> 00:03:42.505
I've realized I can write
down the weird dreams

00:03:42.505 --> 00:03:44.319
that I have about Tina Fey.

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:47.192
- I've been trying to
have a little bit more fun

00:03:47.192 --> 00:03:48.943
with the journal,

00:03:48.943 --> 00:03:51.127
and do drawings and stuff.

00:03:51.127 --> 00:03:56.127
But it also just feels
like a chore, all the time.

00:03:56.228 --> 00:03:58.060
Just like my nightly home work assignment,

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.386
draw in the journal.

00:04:02.476 --> 00:04:04.438
- This one I think you'll enjoy.

00:04:04.438 --> 00:04:06.162
- "I am so overwriting,

00:04:06.162 --> 00:04:08.472
in this damn book, all the time."

00:04:08.472 --> 00:04:09.233
- I quit!

00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:11.323
So I'm not that into journaling.

00:04:11.323 --> 00:04:12.930
What are your reasons you don't like it?

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:14.371
- I write nothing important.

00:04:14.371 --> 00:04:17.532
- It's like, "I bought a projector, today.

00:04:17.532 --> 00:04:18.945
"Let's see how I like it.

00:04:18.945 --> 00:04:21.224
"I've been trying to figure
out the best way to set it up.

00:04:21.224 --> 00:04:22.202
"I need a screen."

00:04:22.202 --> 00:04:24.324
Why did I write that down?

00:04:24.324 --> 00:04:25.494
You know, in retrospect,

00:04:25.494 --> 00:04:27.964
I wish I'd a hired a
journaling ghostwriter.

00:04:27.964 --> 00:04:29.724
- I think the number one thing I learned,

00:04:29.724 --> 00:04:33.385
I don't want to journal to
like, reflect on my life.

00:04:33.385 --> 00:04:34.776
I think it's more fun

00:04:34.776 --> 00:04:37.979
to talk about silly, weird stuff.

00:04:37.979 --> 00:04:40.318
"Red ink. Red book. Red shorts!"

00:04:40.318 --> 00:04:42.525
I was writing this while
wearing red shorts,

00:04:42.525 --> 00:04:44.474
with a red pen, in a red book,

00:04:44.474 --> 00:04:46.057
so I was really excited about that.

00:04:46.057 --> 00:04:47.908
I realized that being looser

00:04:47.908 --> 00:04:51.549
really allowed me to
have more fun with it.

00:04:51.549 --> 00:04:53.204
- Instead of going through Instagram,

00:04:53.204 --> 00:04:54.344
or going on Twitter or whatever,

00:04:54.344 --> 00:04:56.785
I would doodle in my journal for a second,

00:04:56.785 --> 00:04:58.040
and I liked that a lot.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.019
- I learned there's a reason

00:05:00.019 --> 00:05:02.279
I haven't been journaling,
for so many years,

00:05:02.279 --> 00:05:04.373
cuz like journaling is not my fav.

00:05:04.373 --> 00:05:05.320
- I think my big take-away

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.190
was that journaling should
be used as a sketchpad

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.792
for your ideas, and your thoughts.

00:05:08.792 --> 00:05:11.075
A place to let your mind wander.

00:05:11.075 --> 00:05:12.692
- I feel like there'll be
another period after this

00:05:12.692 --> 00:05:14.353
where it'll make sense to journal again.

00:05:14.353 --> 00:05:16.392
- Well I love that my
cat loves the string.

00:05:16.392 --> 00:05:19.069
That's like my favorite thing ever.

00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:20.906
My cat loves journaling,
just as much as I do.

